# Build-time secrets. Both are passed with --secret (BuildKit reads them from
# the host path, NOT the context), so excluding them here does not affect the
# build — it only keeps them out of `COPY . .` and therefore out of the image.
auth.json
docker/env.php.scd
docker/certs
# Runtime env files. These are NOT --secret mounts — nothing in the build reads
# them — so this is the only thing keeping them out of the image, and the
# Dockerfile keeps docker/ in the final stage on purpose (entrypoint.sh reads
# docker/env.php.template). A glob, not a list: docker/.env.production held real
# DB/Valkey/RabbitMQ passwords plus MAGE_CRYPT_KEY and shipped because only
# .env and .env.local were named here. *.example files are safe but excluded
# too — the image never reads them either.
docker/.env*
